{title: 79 Se oye un canto en alta esfera}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{lyricist: Charles Wesley, 1739 (1707-1788); Vers. esp.: Fritz Fliedner (1845-1901)}
{composer: Felix Mendelssohn, 1840 (1809-1847); Arr.: William H. Cummings, 1856 (1831-1915)}

{sov}
[F]Se oye un canto en alta esfera.
"En[C] los[F] cielos[Bb] gloria a[C] Dios[F];
al mortal[C] paz[Dm] en[F] la[C] tierra",
can[Am]ta[G] la celes[C]te[F] voz[G7][C].
[F]Con los[C] cielos alabemos
[F]al e[C]terno Rey[F], can[C]temos
a[Bb] Jesús[D7], a[Gm] nues[D]tro[Gm] Bien,
[C]con el[F] coro de[C] Be[F]lén.
Canta la[Bb] ce[D7]les[Gm]te[Dm] voz[Gm]:
"¡En[C] los[F] cielos[C7] gloria a[F] Dios!"
{eov}

{sov}
[F]El Señor de los señores,
el[C] Un[F]gido celes[Bb]tial[C][F],
a salvar[C] los[Dm] pe[F]ca[C]dores
vi[Am]no[G] al seno[C] vir[F]gi[G7]nal[C].
[F]¡Gloria al[C] Verbo encarnado,
[F]en[C] humani[F]dad[C] velado!
¡Gloria[Bb] al San[D7]to[Gm] de[D] Is[Gm]rael,
[C]cuyo[F] nombre es[C] Ema[F]nuel!
Canta la[Bb] ce[D7]les[Gm]te[Dm] voz[Gm]:
"¡En[C] los[F] cielos[C7] gloria a[F] Dios!"
{eov}

{sov}
[F]Príncipe de paz eterna,
¡gloria[C] a[F] ti, Señor[Bb] Je[C]sús[F]!
Pues al dar[C] tu[Dm] vi[F]da[C] entera
tú[Am] nos[G] traes vi[C]da[F] y[G7] luz[C].
[F]Has tu[C] majestad dejado,
[F]y[C] buscarnos[F] te[C] has dignado;
para[Bb] dar[D7]nos[Gm] el[D] vi[Gm]vir
[C]a la[F] muerte[C] quie[F]res ir.
Canta la[Bb] ce[D7]les[Gm]te[Dm] voz[Gm]:
"¡En[C] los[F] cielos[C7] gloria a[F] Dios!"
{eov}
